        "model": "GPT-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, join an English-speaking group for a visit to Manuel Antonio National Park, in an area of humid tropical forest.\n\nThe park protects primary and secondary forests, mangroves, coastal vegetation, and coral reefs. It is home to about 109 species of mammals, including coatis, two-toed and three-toed sloths, capuchin monkeys, howler monkeys, and jaguars. It also has 184 bird species, including toucans, pelicans, the green kingfisher, and the osprey.\n\nAfter the walk, spend time on the beach, sunbathe, or stroll along the shore.\n\nOvernight at Shana by the Beach Resort. Meals: breakfast."
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:media_alt:ed5d45a8d2a5301f",
